{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/63417-entitlements","id":63417,"title":"Entitlements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-02T07:10:06-08:00","id":63417,"title":"Entitlements","content":"I know that having a Wyrd rating is a prerequisite for joining the documented Entitlements, but is it feasible to have another splat join one with just good rp? And could an Entitlement be made that did not have Wyrd as a rating or is an Entitlement something that is intrinsically linked to the Changeling condition and their magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T13:44:51-08:00","id":63583,"title":"","content":"An Entitlement is the changeling equivalent of a bloodline, so it is intrinsic to the changeling condition. Yes, it is a social group and you can leave it, but the entitlement itself is tied to the Wyrd - otherwise it is just a bunch of changelings hanging out together.<br /> <br /> Now, you lurky bastards, come and blast me on how 75% of vampires are Entitled <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T14:18:14-08:00","id":63595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phalamir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/63417-entitlements?p=63583#post63583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Entitlement is the changeling equivalent of a bloodline, so it is intrinsic to the changeling condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>More analogous to a lodge, actually.<br /> <br /> That said, let's look at how entitlements work:<br /> <br /> Joining a noble order takes up a vow in roughly the same way that joining a Court does; there are in fact a handful of entitlements that have Mantle prerequisites, which immediately disqualifies non-changelings from joining them. Seeing as non-changelings seem to be primarily limited in pledge use by their inability to swear oaths on their own and a noble order presumably wouldn't be bearing the load of witnessing its members own pledges for something as internalized as taking on a title\u2026<br /> <br /> Joining a noble order alters your fae mien, and in some cases this alteration is part and parcel of the entitlement's benefits, like the Legacy of the Black Apple's Black Apple Pendants.<br /> <br /> A number of the privileges of joining a noble order don't make sense for non-changelings \u2014 the Solstice Court's modification of Glamour harvesting and bedlam, for example, or the Gild of Goldspinners' Gildwheel Pledges. Those that don't present this problem \u2014 most of the pure &quot;members can purchase this token&quot; varieties, for instance \u2014 still mainly present the problem that the only benefit of joining could be as easily maintained by simply being well-trusted by/allied to a member of the entitlement; anyone can use a token if they don't mind dealing with both the catch and the drawback, but some entitlement tokens have fairly problematic catches, like the Gildwheel's expensive cost in blood.<br /> <br /> So no, noble orders function off of fae metaphysics and consequently only work for changelings (and possibly bizarre edge-cases one could hang a plothook on).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}